course: dictionary
lesson: 15175
title: Scrumptious and delicious
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Scrumptious is an informal word that means extremely tasty. When you call a cake scrumptious, you mean it tastes wonderful and you want another bite. «Grandma's apple crumble was scrumptious.» The word tells you how the crumble tasted.
explain: Context helps you check the meaning. «Dad made scrumptious pancakes, and we ate them all before breakfast was over.» The pancakes vanished quickly, so they must have been very tasty. Try the swap: delicious fits the sentence, so scrumptious means something like delicious.
explain: Scrumptious can also describe something very attractive or delightful, not just food. «The little puppy had a scrumptious smile.» Here it shows the smile was lovely and charming. The main meaning, though, is about yummy food, and that is where you will meet it most.
explain: Scrumptious is fun to say, and writers like it because it makes food sound amazing. Because it is informal, you would use it when talking with friends or in a story, not usually in a formal letter.
fact: Scrumptious is an informal word, so it is used in everyday talk and stories.
fact: «Scrumptious» means extremely tasty and delicious.
fact: «Scrumptious» can also mean very attractive or delightful.
fact: Phrases you may hear are «scrumptious food» and «absolutely scrumptious».
fact: Its other forms are more scrumptious and most scrumptious.
exercise: «The chocolate cake was scrumptious.» What does scrumptious mean? | Hard to lift | Cold and wet | *Extremely tasty | Very heavy
exercise: «We ate scrumptious sandwiches at the picnic.» Which word is closest in meaning? | *Delicious | Noisy | Empty | Muddy
exercise: Ella says scrumptious is a formal word used in school reports. Is she right? | Yes, but only for talking about the weather | Yes, it is only for school reports | *No, it is informal and used in everyday talk and stories | No, it means very cold
test: «The cook made a scrumptious stew for the whole family.» What does scrumptious describe? | *Tasty food | Heavy plate | Broken spoon | Dark kitchen
test: Jay says, «Her scrumptious smile made everyone happy.» What does scrumptious mean here? | Angry and loud | *Charming and delightful | Tired and sleepy | Cold and grey
exam: Read «The bakery smelled scrumptious, so we bought three buns.» What does scrumptious tell you about the buns? | Expensive | Stale | *They looked and smelled very tasty | Tiny
